---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy · Alliance Mutual Escrow"
  description="What the Alliance Mutual Escrow website collects and what it never does: no ad tracking, no selling data, calculator use is anonymous."
  kicker="Your information"
  heading="Privacy"
  draft={true}
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site is built to know as little about you as possible. The fee calculator runs in your
    browser and sends nothing unless you ask it to. There is no advertising tracking and we do not
    sell or share visitor data.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site collects</h2>
  <p>
    <b>Nothing you type in the calculator</b> leaves your browser, except when you choose "email me
    this estimate": then your email address and the estimate are sent once, used to send that one
    message, and not stored by the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Standard server logs.</b> Our host (Cloudflare) keeps ordinary technical logs, such as IP
    addresses and requested pages, for security and reliability.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Privacy-friendly analytics.</b> If analytics are enabled, they are cookie-free and aggregate:
    page counts, not people. No cross-site tracking, no profiles.
  </p>

  <h2>Escrow files are different</h2>
  <p>
    When you open an escrow with us, the file itself contains real financial information. That
    information is governed by California escrow law and our regulatory obligations, is used only to
    close your transaction, and is never sold. This page covers the website; your officer can answer
    questions about the file.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href="mailto:info@ameescrow.com" style="color:var(--amber)">info@ameescrow.com</a> and a person will answer.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
